  "articleBody": "Getting a room ready for new drywall installation is more than just clearing out furniture; it's about setting the stage for a successful, long-lasting finish. Here's a quick checklist to help you out:\n\n1.  **Clear the Space:** Move all furniture, decorations, and anything else out of the room. Cover floors with drop cloths, especially if you're working on an existing structure, to protect them from dust and debris.\n2.  **Inspect Framing:** Check all studs and joists for any damage, rot, or warping. Ensure they are plumb and level. Any issues here will translate directly to your finished walls.\n3.  **Check Utilities:** Make sure all electrical wiring, plumbing, and HVAC ducts are properly installed, secured, and inspected if required by local codes. You don't want to cut into a live wire later!\n4.  **Insulation:** If insulation is needed, install it before hanging drywall. Ensure it's properly fitted and vapor barriers are in place where necessary.\n5.  **Mark Studs:** Clearly mark the location of all studs on the ceiling and floor. This will make fastening your drywall much easier and more accurate.\n6.  **Gather Tools & Materials:** Have your drywall sheets, screws, cutting tools, and lifts ready. This prevents interruptions once you start hanging.\n\nTaking the time for thorough preparation can prevent costly mistakes and ensure a much smoother installation process. If you're in areas like Castle Rock or Elizabeth and need a hand with a major remodel, we're here to ensure everything is set up perfectly.",
